title: AlexStart
---
<<declare $npcName2 = "Alex">> //The NPC's name will go here and can be different for each NPC if needed

{$npcName2}: Much like Johnny, I don't have a welcome, but I might in the future.
-> <i>Ask about their day</i>
    <<jump AlexDay>>
-> <i>Back to the lobby</i>
===

title: AlexDay
---
{$npcName2}: Sorry, my day hasn't been the best. I don't really want to get into it, but it's just one of those days you'd rather want to get through already.
-> Cheer up! Things'll get better.
    <<jump AlexGood>>
-> Is everything alright?
    <<jump AlexNeutral>>
-> We all have those days. //This may be the case where the dialogue may need changing to fit the outcome or may not have an actual bad outcome
    <<jump AlexBad>>
===

title: AlexGood
---
{$npcName2}: Thanks, I always try to find light at the end of the tunnel.
===

title: AlexNeutral
---
{$npcName2}: Sorry, as I said, I really don't want to get into it right now.
===

title: AlexBad
---
{$npcName2}: We do, and we all wish we didn't.
===